    "description": "Engineer Sr --- October 2011 – November 2015\n \n•\tWorked in test software development supporting the testing of FC HBAs and FC, FCoE, iSCSI Converged Network Adapters\n•\tResponsible for the development and maintenance of tools to assist the greater test team, as well as development and execution of automated tests\n•\tDeveloped external utilities for interacting with HP Quality Center, including automated posting of test results, report generation and data export to MS Excel\n•\tDeveloped major components of a Java based Data Integrity tool used in most of our team’s testing\n•\tCo-developed a new Ruby based test automation framework suited to the current testing environments\n•\tTrained new employees on the test procedures and the maintenance and execution of tools and tests for the Bridge products\n\n\nTest Engineer Sr --- October 2010 – September 2011\nTest Engineer ------- October 2008 – September 2010 \n \n•\tTesting Lead for FC-SATA, FC-SAS and SAS-SATA Bridge products\n•\tWorked as part of the test automation development team for these products\n•\tResponsibilities included triage of regression testing failures, filing FW bug reports, maintenance of the automated tests and development of new automated tests to cover new FW features\n•\tDeveloped new features in the automation testing framework to simplify its maintenance and support\n•\tDeveloped a new more efficient regression testing triage process to allow faster turnaround on bug fixes by facilitating the timely exchange of information between customer, firmware developer and tester\n•\tDeveloped new tools to automate much of the failure analysis and triage process\n\n \nAssociate Test Engineer --- July 2007 – September 2008 \n\n•\tOne of two testers on a support team for an FC-SATA Router product\n•\tResponsible for bug reproduction to assist FW developers\n•\tPerformed Regression testing on FW releases \n•\tIncreased testing performance by automating tedious test setup tasks",
